# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lowering shared by every query in scripts/formal.sh.
#
# The caller has already read the design and run `hierarchy` with the geometry
# it wants to check, so this file must not do either -- it would undo the
# -chparam overrides the caller just applied.
#
# Every line here is the fix for a specific way the first attempt failed. They
# are recorded rather than folded away because none of them is guessable from
# the yosys command reference alone.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `sat` solves one module. Without flattening, the properties that live inside
# out_fifo and tile_ctrl are simply not part of the problem, and the proof comes
# back green having checked two of the seven.
prep -top systolic_tile -flatten

# `sat` has no memory model. The accumulator bank and the FIFO storage have to
# become ordinary registers before the solver can see through them -- which is
# why MAX_M, not ROWS or COLS, is the parameter that decides whether this
# terminates in seconds or never.
memory_map

# The design resets asynchronously. `sat` reasons about synchronous state only,
# and refuses to lower an edge-triggered assertion until the reset is
# synchronous: "Cannot lower edge triggered $check cell, run async2sync or
# clk2fflogic first."
async2sync

# Two commands are deliberately missing from the end of this file, and
# scripts/formal.sh appends them instead:
#
#   chformal -lower   Yosys 0.39 and later keep SystemVerilog assertions as
#                     $check cells, which the SAT solver cannot import ("Failed
#                     to import cell ... (type $check) to SAT database"). This
#                     turns them back into the $assert cells -prove-asserts
#                     reads. Older builds -- including the yosys in Ubuntu
#                     24.04 -- emit $assert directly and reject the option, so
#                     the driver asks `help chformal` and only adds it if the
#                     tool understands it.
#   opt -full         has to follow the lowering, not precede it.
